export anchor EncyclopediaStyle:
    number: 40
    screen: ProjectDetail
    name: Encyclopedia
    idea: The project reads like a reference article, with a lead paragraph, a summary infobox on the right, a contents box, serif headings over thin rules, blue links and bracketed citations.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f6f6f6, the area around the article and the side nav
        sheet: #ffffff, the article body
        text: #202122, body text and headings
        muted: #54595d, the tagline, captions and side nav headings
        linkBlue: #1d52a3, links, the primary button, the progress ring and the focus outline
        rule: #a2a9b1, heading underlines and box borders
        box: #f8f9fa, the infobox, the contents box and tables
        band: #dde6f3, infobox group header rows
        green: #1e6b35, the On track and Done words
        red: #a3221b, the Blocked word
    type:
        Headings use a serif, "Linux Libertine", Georgia, Times, serif, at
        28px for the title and 22px for section heads, both regular weight.
        Body uses a system sans, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica,
        Arial, sans-serif, at 15px with 1.6 line height. The infobox
        caption is 16px bold sans, infobox rows, contents and references
        are 13px, and citation marks are 11px superscript.
    layout:
        A white top bar holds a line emblem, the Brightwork name with a
        tagline, a wide search field with a Search button, and the user
        links. Under it a 170px plain side nav lists Navigation, Design team
        and Tools links on the grey page. The white article sheet has view
        tabs Project and Discussion on the left, and Read, Edit and View
        history on the right. The title sits over a thin rule with a from
        line. The infobox floats right at 290px with a progress ring, then
        grouped rows for Project, Dates and People. The lead paragraph holds
        the brief, then a collapsible contents box, then sections
        Milestones as a bordered table, Open tasks as a bullet list, Files,
        Discussion as a quote, and References. Each section head has an
        edit link at the right. Below 860px the side nav hides and the
        infobox spans the full width above the text.
    spacing: 16 to 24px article padding, 22px above section heads and 10px between paragraphs.
    density: Medium dense reading text, with the facts compressed into the infobox.
    corners: Square boxes. Buttons and fields have 2px corners.
    borders: A 1px grey rule under every heading. 1px boxes round the infobox, the contents box and the table cells.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Almost none. Status uses text marks with words, a tick for Done and
        On track, a half circle for In progress, an open circle for Planned
        and a slashed circle for Blocked. A simple line emblem sits beside
        the brand.
    focus: A 2px link blue outline offset 1px. A focused field gets a blue border with an inset ring.
    tone: Neutral encyclopedic third person, such as Website redesign is a project of the Design team.
